data: {"item_id":"rs_861621","output_index":0,"sequence_number":603,"summary_index":0,"text":"Okay, so I need to calculate 17 multiplied by 23. Let me think about how to do this. Hmm, multiplication. Maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier.\n\nFirst, I remember that 17 times 20 is 340, because 10 times 20 is 200, 7 times , wait no, maybe better to do 17*20. Let's see, 10*20 is 200, 7*20 is 140, so 200+140 is 340. Yeah, that's right. So 17*20 = 340.\n\nThen, 17 times 3 is 51. Because 10*3=30, 7*3=21, so 30+21=51.\n\nSo adding those two results together: 340 + 51. Let me add that. 340 + 50 is 390, then +1 is 391. So 391?\n\nWait, is that correct? Let me check another way to make sure. Maybe using another method.\n\nAlternatively, 23 times 17. Let's do 20*17 = 340, and 3*17 = 51, so same as before. 340 +51=391. Hmm, same answer.\n\nWait, another way: (20 + 3) * 17 = 20*17 + 3*17 = 340 + 51 = 391. Yeah, that's the same.\n\nOr maybe using distributive property in another way. Let's see, 17*23 = (10 + 7)*(20 + 3). Hmm, expanding that might be more complicated, but let's try.\n\n10*20 = 200\n\n10*3 = 30\n\n7*20 = 140\n\n7*3 = 21\n\nAdd them all up: 200 +30 = 230, 230 +140 = 370, 370 +21 = 391. Okay, same result.\n\nAlternatively, use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n    23\n\n  x17\n\n------\n\nFirst multiply 23 by 7: 23*7 = 161\n\nThen multiply 23 by 10 (since it's the 1 in the tens place): 230\n\nAdd them together: 161 + 230 = 391\n\nYes, that's","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

